{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Shomer</b> — the meaning is that I do not devise stratagems to escape, for I have set my soul like one of the simpletons, for if I am impoverished — I know that HaShem, who is gracious and compassionate, will save me, and I would bring tidings to my soul, saying to it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:47.663604500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}